<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%- include('partials/head') %>
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('partials/header') %>

  <div class="legal-page">
    <button type="button" class="legal-back" data-legal-back>&larr; Back</button>
    <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: <%= new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-IN', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' }) %></p>

    <p>
      At Kalpavruksha Kalyana, we value your privacy and are committed to protecting your
      personal information. This Cookie Policy explains what cookies and similar technologies
      we use, why we use them, and how you can control them. It forms part of our
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>1. What Cookies Are</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies are small text files placed on your device when you visit a website. They allow a
        site to remember information about you between page loads, so you do not have to re-enter
        the same details each time you visit.
      </p>
      <p>
        Similar technologies include web storage APIs such as <strong>localStorage</strong> and
        <strong>sessionStorage</strong>. We refer to all of these collectively as "cookies" in this
        policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. Cookies We Use</h2>
      <p>We currently use the following cookies on our website:</p>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>
          <strong>kalpavruksha_sid</strong> &mdash; A session cookie that keeps you signed in while
          you browse the platform. It contains only an opaque session identifier and carries no
          personal information.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>kalpavruksha_csrf</strong> &mdash; A security cookie used to protect forms and
          sign-in activity against cross-site request forgery (CSRF). It contains a random value
          only and carries no personal information.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>lang</strong> &mdash; Remembers whether you chose to view the site in English or
          Kannada, so the language does not reset on every visit.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>cookie_consent</strong> &mdash; Records your cookie choice (all cookies, or
          essential cookies only) so we do not ask you again on every visit.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. How We Use Cookies</h2>
      <p>Our website uses cookies to:</p>
      <ul class="legal-list">
        <li>Keep you signed in and remember your preferences.</li>
        <li>Protect your account and our forms from security threats.</li>
        <li>Improve website performance and reliability.</li>
        <li>Analyse website traffic and understand how the site is used.</li>
        <li>Enhance your overall browsing experience.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not use cookies to collect personally identifiable information for advertising
        purposes, and we do not sell your cookie data to third parties.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Essential and Non-Essential Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Essential cookies</strong> are required for the website to function correctly &mdash;
        for example, signing you in, keeping your session active, and protecting forms from
        cross-site request forgery. These are always active and cannot be switched off, because the
        platform would not work without them.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Non-essential cookies</strong> are those used for optional purposes such as traffic
        analysis and enhanced browsing features. These are only set if you accept them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Kalpavruksha Kalyana does not use advertising, cross-site tracking, or behavioural
        profiling cookies. If optional analytics or similar features are introduced in future, they
        will remain switched off until you give your consent.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. Managing Your Cookie Preferences</h2>
      <p>
        You may disable cookies through your browser settings, although some features of the
        website may not function properly if you do so. In particular, blocking essential cookies
        will prevent you from signing in or submitting any form on the site.
      </p>
      <p>
        To change or withdraw your choice, you can clear the <strong>cookie_consent</strong> cookie
        in your browser settings &mdash; this will cause the consent banner to appear again the next
        time you visit, so you can select a different option. You can also re-open this banner at any
        time using the "Cookie Settings" link in the footer.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most browsers can be configured to block all or specific cookies, or to prompt you before
        accepting them. Please consult your browser's help documentation for instructions.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. Third-Party Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Some pages may embed content or links from third-party websites, which may set their own
        cookies under their own privacy policies. We do not control or govern these cookies. We
        recommend reviewing the privacy policies of any third-party site you visit.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. Your Consent</h2>
      <p>
        Where consent is required, it is collected through the cookie banner shown on your first
        visit to the site. You may withdraw consent at any time using the "Cookie Settings" link in
        the footer or by clearing your browser cookies for this site.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>8. Children</h2>
      <p>
        Our services are intended only for individuals who are legally eligible to marry under
        applicable law. We do not knowingly collect personal information or set cookies for the
        purpose of building profiles on children.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>9. Changes to This Cookie Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page
        with the revised effective date. Continued use of the website after such changes
        constitutes acceptance of the updated Cookie Policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For any questions about cookies or this Cookie Policy, please reach out via the Contact
        section on our home page. For our full privacy practices, please see our
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <%- include('partials/footer') %>

  <%- include('partials/legal-back-script') %>
</body>
</html>
